Description: Serve the SM8750 sensors PD (Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro)
 The sensors PD of the piano ADSP firmware needs more of the remote file
 system than hexagonrpcd serves for older SoCs:
 .
  - it reads its JSON configuration from /odm/etc/sensors/config, next to
    the /vendor path;
  - it writes the sensors registry back to /mnt/vendor/persist/sensors
    (temporary file, then rename), so fopen in "w"/"a" mode, fwrite and
    frename (extended method 33) are served for that one directory, into
    the copy named by HEXAGONRPC_PERSIST_DIR; nothing else is writable and
    ".." is refused;
  - it calls extended apps_std methods (ids >= 31 arrive as method 31 with
    the real id in the first input word), e.g. fopen_with_env_fd (36),
    which is answered with ENOENT;
  - it passes input buffers larger than 256 bytes, fetched with
    adsp_listener get_in_bufs2.
 .
 An unsupported extended call is answered with AEE_EUNSUPPORTED instead of
 ending the listener loop, which used to stop the daemon silently.
Author: piano mainline contributors
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-29
